    "since": "3.21.0",
    "capability": "tasks.assignProjectAgent",
    "note": "assignee kind new_project_agent puts a new worker on the task's own project's conversation, beside its pinned coordinator, and hands it the task; it works in the project's original sources, so the dispatch names no workspace. It takes agent_name, provider, model, effort, role, capability and notify_user like new_agent, and no project: the project is the task's. operation_id is the client's id for the assignment: the delivery is queued under it, and asking again with the same id answers the dispatch the task already records, delivering nothing and making no agent a second time. The same id asked of a different assignment of the task is conflict.",
